<title>UK: Saudi cuts May crude to U.S. by 15-25 cents.</title>
<headline>Saudi cuts May crude to U.S. by 15-25 cents.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>State Saudi Aramco cut crude formula prices for May sales to U.S. buyers by 15-25 cents a barrel from April levels, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Aramco told customers May liftings for Arab Light would be priced at WTI less $3.60 a barrel, down 15 cents from April.  </p>
<p>May Arab Heavy was reduced by 15 cents to WTI less $5.50 a barrel.</p>
<p>May extra light Berri was cut by 25 cents to WTI less $2.60 a barrel.</p>
<p>All prices are free on board (fob) Ras Tanura.</p>
<p>Saudi Arab Medium prices for May were not immediately available.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
</text>
